# No admin ops in public UI

Public Hub pages (dApps, Games, Tokens, Store, etc.) must never expose operator / deploy / env setup status.

## Forbidden in public UI

- Env var names (`NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, `process.env`, “Set NEXT_PUBLIC_…”)
- Phrases like “Pending ops”, “Not configured”, “Vault not configured”, “awaiting watcher”, “redeploy”
- Internal ops checklists, mint-watcher status for operators, or secrets/treasury setup hints

## Do this instead

- Show only user-facing facts: fee, direction, live vault address (when set), network, version.
- If a vault / covenant / feature is not ready: omit the box, or show a short user line (“Coming soon”) without env or ops detail.
- Keep operator docs in `docs/` or private runbooks, not in Metadata tabs or widget banners.

## Metadata boxes

Never push a `HubMetadataStat` whose value or hint is an env instruction or ops pending state.
